# The necromancer's legion (WP-N2: necro/legion.js, necro/legion_commands.js, design/data/necro.toml). `ttl necro legion
# expect`, `ttl roads expect` and `ttl rep expect` print "ttl: ..." when wrong, which `server.sh test-all` counts as a failure.
# A is the necromancer at a Bone Altar on a platform far from every NPC; B is a second Life 2 soul (the PvP victim and the
# corpse). The rank is a test hook (WP-N3's Rite is not needed). Expect in the log: "[ttl] legion: TtlBotNecroA raised #<n>
# skeleton (dust)", "... raised Death Knight #<n> (ash, corpse of TtlBotNecroB)", "... #<n> of TtlBotNecroA fell (death)".
# Verify in game (first run): `owner_set` (Tensura's permanent owner took), `named` after `tensura edit owner ... name set`.
ttlbot spawn TtlBotNecroA
ttlbot spawn TtlBotNecroB
@sleep 3
ttl reset TtlBotNecroA
ttl reset TtlBotNecroB
@sleep 3
ttl necro legion test TtlBotNecroA reset
ttl necro legion test TtlBotNecroB reset
ttl necro legion test TtlBotNecroA servercap -1
# The platform at 4400 lies outside the canon continent, where only the soul's own karma is paid (R11): the test
# counts it as inside (the Church's Sense hook, necro.js), so the roads pay rep, balance and renown in full.
ttl necro test TtlBotNecroA continent 1
ttl roads test TtlBotNecroA reset
# Life 1: nothing answers.
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA try_raise_dust life2only
ttl roads test TtlBotNecroA life2
ttl roads test TtlBotNecroB life2
gamemode creative TtlBotNecroA
gamemode creative TtlBotNecroB
execute in minecraft:overworld run forceload add 4390 4390 4420 4410
execute in minecraft:overworld run fill 4390 150 4390 4420 150 4410 minecraft:stone
execute in minecraft:overworld run fill 4390 151 4390 4420 156 4410 minecraft:air
execute in minecraft:overworld run setblock 4400 151 4400 ttl:bone_altar
execute in minecraft:overworld run tp TtlBotNecroA 4402 151 4400
execute in minecraft:overworld run tp TtlBotNecroB 4410 151 4400
@sleep 1
# 1. No altar of one's own, then no rank: refused with the right reason.
ttl necro legion test TtlBotNecroA rank 1
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA try_raise_dust noaltar
ttl necro legion altar TtlBotNecroA 4400 151 4400
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA altars 1
ttl necro legion test TtlBotNecroA rank 0
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA try_raise_dust norank
ttl necro legion test TtlBotNecroA rank 1
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA try_raise_dust nodust
# 2. The grey road: 4 bone dust a legionnaire, Tensura's own undead with a permanent owner; rank 1 holds 2 awake.
give TtlBotNecroA ttl:bone_dust 12
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA try_raise_dust ok
execute as TtlBotNecroA run ttl necro raise skeleton dust
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA last ok
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA awake 1
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA entities 1
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA owner_set 1
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA points 1
ttl roads expect TtlBotNecroA count_necro.raise.grey 1
ttl roads expect TtlBotNecroA chaos2 0
execute as TtlBotNecroA run ttl necro raise zombie
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA awake 2
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA dust 4
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA try_raise_dust cap
execute as TtlBotNecroA run ttl necro raise skeleton dust
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA last cap
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA awake 2
# 3. Sleep: NBT into the record, no entity left; wake: back at the altar, still bound.
execute as TtlBotNecroA run ttl necro stow all
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA awake 0
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA dormant 2
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA entities 0
execute as TtlBotNecroA run ttl necro rouse all
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA awake 2
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA dormant 0
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA entities 2
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA owner_set 2
# 4. Naming is Tensura's own (here its op command): a named legionnaire counts for the army.
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA named 0
execute in minecraft:overworld positioned 4400 152 4400 run tensura edit owner @e[tag=ttl.legion,limit=1,sort=nearest] name set Bonesworth
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA named 1
execute as TtlBotNecroA run ttl necro muster
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA army 1
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA muster no
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA cap 2
# 5. The dark road: soul ash, x1.5, and the five costs through TtlRoads (karma, the Church).
ttl necro legion test TtlBotNecroA rank 2
ttl rep set TtlBotNecroA holy_church 0
give TtlBotNecroA ttl:soul_ash 1
execute as TtlBotNecroA run ttl necro raise skeleton ash Ashborn
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA awake 3
ttl roads expect TtlBotNecroA count_necro.raise.dark 1
ttl roads expect TtlBotNecroA chaos2 3
ttl rep expect TtlBotNecroA holy_church value -3
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA ash 0
# 6. The PvP owner rule: outside arenas, wars and PvP quests the dead never hurt a soul.
ttl necro legion pvp TtlBotNecroA TtlBotNecroB
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA pvp_TtlBotNecroB refused
# 7. Soul ash from a player kill (O-N4): once per victim per 24 h; the kill leaves a corpse for a Death Knight (O-N6).
ttl necro legion test TtlBotNecroA rank 3
give TtlBotNecroA tensura:high_magisteel_helmet
give TtlBotNecroA tensura:high_magisteel_chestplate
give TtlBotNecroA tensura:high_magisteel_leggings
give TtlBotNecroA tensura:high_magisteel_boots
give TtlBotNecroA tensura:high_magisteel_sword
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA try_knight_ash noash
ttl necro legion corpse TtlBotNecroA TtlBotNecroB arena
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA ash 1
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA corpses 1
ttl necro legion corpse TtlBotNecroA TtlBotNecroB arena
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA ash 1
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA try_knight_ash ok
execute as TtlBotNecroA run ttl necro knight Alberto ash
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA last ok
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA knights 1
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA corpses 0
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA awake 4
ttl roads expect TtlBotNecroA count_necro.knight.dark 1
# rank 3 holds one knight
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA try_knight_dust knightcap
# 8. A fallen knight never rises again.
kill @e[tag=ttl.knight]
@sleep 2
ttl necro legion sweep
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA knights 0
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA fallen 1
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA awake 3
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA try_rouse_fallen fallen
# 9. The server cap (O-N3): above it a raise waits in the queue and rises when another sleeps.
ttl necro legion test TtlBotNecroA servercapnow
give TtlBotNecroA ttl:bone_dust 4
execute as TtlBotNecroA run ttl necro raise zombie dust
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA last queued
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA queue 1
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA awake 3
# a bare altar has 2 niches: two of the three lie down, and the queued zombie rises at once
execute as TtlBotNecroA run ttl necro stow all
@sleep 1
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA queue 0
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA awake 2
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA dormant 2
ttl necro legion info TtlBotNecroA
# 10. The Keeper's road: a grave marker laid to rest pays the good road once a day per marker.
execute in minecraft:overworld run setblock 4403 151 4402 ttl:grave_marker
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA try_rest ok
execute as TtlBotNecroA run ttl necro rest
ttl roads expect TtlBotNecroA count_necro.rest.good 1
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA try_rest rested
# Clean up.
ttl necro legion test TtlBotNecroA servercap -1
ttl necro legion test TtlBotNecroA reset
ttl necro legion test TtlBotNecroB reset
ttl necro legion expect TtlBotNecroA entities 0
execute in minecraft:overworld run fill 4390 151 4390 4420 156 4410 minecraft:air
execute in minecraft:overworld run forceload remove 4390 4390 4420 4410
ttl roads test TtlBotNecroA reset
ttl necro test TtlBotNecroA continent 0
ttl reset TtlBotNecroA
ttl reset TtlBotNecroB
ttlbot remove TtlBotNecroA
ttlbot remove TtlBotNecroB
